<title>CROATIA: Croatian Dec currency reserves fall to $4.30 bln.</title>
<headline>Croatian Dec currency reserves fall to $4.30 bln.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Croatia issued the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> CROATIA CURRENCY RESERVES  DEC '96     NOV '96     DEC '95</p>
<p> Total (million USD)	  4,306.1     4,342.7     3,264.7</p>
<p> National Bank of Croatia   2,314.0     2,292.5     1,895.2</p>
<p> Commercial banks	     1,992.1     2,050.2     1,369.5 NOTE</p>
<p>-- Commercial banks' December currency reserves shrank 2.8 percent after a 1.3-percent monthly fall in November.</p>
<p>The central bank's international reserves rose 0.9 percent after shrinking 0.9 percent in November. They represented more than 3-1/2 months worth of 1996 imports.</p>
<p>-- Kolumbina Bencevic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
